      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f46b08e0effe3cdmx6k0Uon2jw\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n# A2E Realtime Gateway — Self-Hosting Requirements\n\n## 1. WebSocket path / port\n- Path is `/realtime` — `REALTIME_WS_PATH` at `realtime-gateway.constants.ts:3`. Client builds `ws(s)://<SERVER_URL>/realtime` from `REACT_APP_SERVER_BASE_URL` (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/realtime/constants/RealtimeConstants.ts:7-9`); mirror enum `ApiPath.Realtime = 'realtime'` (`twenty-shared/src/types/ApiPath.ts:6`).\n- Raw `ws` server (`WebSocketServer`, `noServer: true`) is attached to the Nest HTTP server's `upgrade` event on the **same port as the API** (`NODE_PORT`, default 3000) — `realtime-gateway.service.ts:105-163`; port default `config-variables.ts:1463`. No separate WS port in any compose/manifest.\n\n## 2. Redis\n- **Required.** Compose pins `redis:7` with `--maxmemory-policy noeviction`, healthcheck `redis-cli ping` (`packages/twenty-docker/docker-compose.yml:127-136`; `docker-compose.coolify.yml:128-136`). No host port published; `server`/`worker` depend on `service_healthy`.\n- **Channel prefix `a2e:rt:`** — `REALTIME_REDIS_CHANNEL_PREFIX` (`realtime-gateway.constants.ts:5`), used in `publish`/`subscribe`/`message` (`realtime-publisher.service.ts:50,65,80,134`). Topics are `workspace:<id>[:kind:scope]` (`parse-realtime-topic.util.ts:8-40`).\n- **Presence TTL keys** in Redis: `presence:<workspaceId>:<userId>` (45 s), `presence-typing:...` (5 s), `presence-connections:...` sorted set — `presence.service.ts:255-265`, constants lines 18-22.\n- **Why:** cross-instance fan-out (server + worker, future replicas) — `realtime-publisher.service.ts:21-23`; `docs/plan/03-integration-blueprint.md:141-145`.\n- **If unavailable:** `publish` logs and swallows the error (`realtime-publisher.service.ts:56-58`); `subscribeTopic` rejects, and the gateway returns an `error` envelope instead of acking (`realtime-publisher.service.ts:81-99`; `realtime-gateway.service.ts:532-538`). Presence ops throw. `/readyz` fails (Redis `PING`) — `readiness.service.ts:39-57`.\n- **Clustering:** client is a single ioredis connection (`new IORedis(redisUrl,{maxRetriesPerRequest:null})`, `redis-client.service.ts:43-45`); no cluster/sentinel code. Optional separate queue connection via `REDIS_QUEUE_URL` (`redis-client.service.ts:20-21`).\n\n## 3. Environment variables (file:line)\n| Var | Default | Read at |\n|---|---|---|\n| `REDIS_URL` | none in code; compose `redis://redis:6379` | `config-variables.ts:1396-1408`, consumed `redis-client.service.ts:37` |\n| `REDIS_QUEUE_URL` (optional) | unset | `config-variables.ts:1410-1424`, `redis-client.service.ts:20` |\n| `SERVER_URL` | `http://localhost:3000` | `config-variables.ts:1490-1498` |\n| `FRONTEND_URL` | unset | `config-variables.ts:1103-1110` |\n| `ENCRYPTION_KEY` | optional, falls back to `APP_SECRET` | `config-variables.ts:1567-1576` |\n| `APP_SECRET` | compose falls back to `ENCRYPTION_KEY` | `config-variables.ts:1558-1565`; `docker-compose.coolify.yml:37,86` |\n| `AUTH_COOKIE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | `''` | `config-variables.ts:407-414` |\n| `SERVER_KEEP_ALIVE_TIMEOUT_MS` | `65000` | `config-variables.ts:1477`, applied `main.ts:105-111` |\n| `TRUST_PROXY` | `loopback, linklocal, uniquelocal` | `config-variables.ts:1515` |\n| `WORKER_HEALTH_PORT` | `3099` | `start-worker-health-server.ts:7,17-19` |\n\nOrigins/CORS: `SERVER_URL` + `FRONTEND_URL` + `AUTH_COOKIE_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (`resolve-allowed-credentialed-origins.util.ts:61-67`); WS upgrade uses the same policy + `x-forwarded-proto` (`realtime-gateway.service.ts:119-152`).\n\n## 4. Reverse proxy\n- Must forward `Upgrade`/`Connection` on `/realtime` on the API port (same host).\n- Server pings every 15 s and terminates without pong (`REALTIME_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS`, gateway 165-179), so the proxy idle/read timeout must exceed ~30 s; keep-alive default 65 s intentionally exceeds proxy idle (`config-variables.ts:1467-1477`).\n- SSE/streaming: GraphQL subscriptions (`EventStreamResolver`) for MCP/db events coexist on the HTTP API (`repository-architecture-audit.md:121,189`); proxy must not buffer streams.\n- **Gap:** shipped ingress has **no** WS/timeout annotations (`k8s/manifests/ingress.yaml`; Helm `values.yaml:72` empty). Self-hosters must add them.\n\n## 5. Documented limitations\n- Redis pub/sub is **fan-out, not a replay log** (`realtime-publisher.service.ts:21-23`; `repository-architecture-audit.md:189-193,492`; blueprint `146-150`).\n- `seq` is per-socket/topic, reset on reconnect — not a durable cursor (`realtime-gateway.service.ts:486-506`).\n- Client: exponential backoff, 10 attempts, 500 ms→30 s, full resubscribe on open (`RealtimeConstants.ts:11-15`; `realtimeConnectionManager.ts:206-268`). Ephemeral/at-most-once; failed subscribe must not ack. `REALTIME_RECONNECT_RESUME_WINDOW_MS`/`REALTIME_RESUME_WINDOW_MS` (30 s) are defined but I found **no consumer** — treat as unused (uncertain).\n\n## 6. Worker\nWorker (`worker:prod`) needs Redis for BullMQ and imports `CoreEngineModule` → `RealtimeGatewayModule` (`queue-worker.module.ts:10-11`; `core-engine.module.ts:182`). With no HTTP adapter the gateway no-ops (`realtime-gateway.service.ts:85-95`), so **no WS port**; but `NotificationModule` is loaded and can publish `a2e:rt:*` from jobs. Worker readiness on 3099 checks DB+Redis.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
