        "prompt": "Research only, do NOT modify any files.\n\nIn the repo /Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite, I need accurate self-hosting requirements for the A2E realtime gateway (WebSocket) and its Redis dependency.\n\nInspect:\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/realtime-gateway/` (all files: constants, module, services, utils, types)\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/redis-client/` (config/env var names, defaults, clustering)\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/twenty-config/` for Redis/CORS/HTTP-related env var names and defaults (search for REDIS_URL, ENCRYPTION_KEY, SERVER_URL, FRONTEND_URL, CORS, etc.)\n- `packages/twenty-docker/` (docker-compose files, Dockerfiles, SELF-HOSTING.md) for redis service/version, ports, healthchecks, and any proxy/Traefik config\n- `DEPLOY.md` for the current deployment guidance\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/realtime/` (constants/RealtimeConstants.ts, RealtimeConnectionManager) to confirm the client URL derivation (ws:// same origin `/realtime`)\n\nProduce a factual summary for a self-host doc section about gateway requirements. Include:\n1. The WebSocket path and that it runs on the same HTTP port as the API.\n2. Redis: required, version used by compose, the channel prefix used for pub/sub, why it is needed (cross-instance fan-out, presence TTL keys), and behavior if Redis is unavailable.\n3. Exact environment variable names and defaults that a self-hoster must set (REDIS_URL, SERVER_URL, ENCRYPTION_KEY, etc.), and where they are read in code (file:line).\n4. Reverse-proxy requirements: WebSocket upgrade headers, long-lived connection timeouts, SSE endpoint too if relevant.\n5. Any documented limitations (Redis pub/sub is not a replay log, reconnect behavior, at-most-once).\n6. Whether worker process needs Redis/realtime.\nReport exact file paths and symbol names. Do not speculate; flag uncertainty. Keep it under ~600 words.",
        "endedAt": "2026-09-19T10:57:51.574Z",
